    {
      "title": "Incident review — checkout timeouts",
      "description": "A blameless write-up of last week's 38-minute checkout degradation: timeline, contributing factors and the follow-ups that actually close it.",
      "brief": "## Incident review — checkout timeouts\n\n**Severity** SEV-2 · **Duration** 38 min · **Customer impact** ~6% of checkouts timed out\n**Review** @+2d, 30 min, blameless\n\n### Summary\nA connection-pool change in the payments service went out with the default pool size of 10 instead of 50. Under the evening peak the pool saturated, requests queued, and the checkout gateway timed out at 5s.\n\n### Why it got past us\n- The config change was in a shared library bump, not a payments PR\n- Staging traffic never exceeds the smaller pool\n- The saturation alert existed but routed to a muted channel\n\n### What this desk is for\nOne place for the timeline, the evidence and the follow-ups, so the review is about decisions rather than reconstructing what happened.",
      "callout": {
        "title": "The one follow-up that matters",
        "body": "Pool size moves out of the shared library and into service config, with a startup check that refuses to boot below the floor. Everything else is a nice-to-have.",
        "accent": "#10b981",
        "icon": "✅"
      },
